    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required exposing a `checkDigit` field on the owner API \u2014 a single Luhn check digit over the digits of the `customerCode`. I implemented it in three small, low-impact touches:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny, cohesive utility class with a single static `of(String)` method that computes the Luhn digit. Putting it in its own class keeps its surrounding complexity (`WMC_other`) at the floor of 1, rather than paying for the whole `OwnerMapper` class had I added the loop there.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` line delegating `checkDigit` to `CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`, following the exact pattern already used for `householdId`, `identityKey`, `locality`, etc. The changed method (`toOwnerDto`) is a bodyless interface declaration, so the edit is a single line against a CC-1 method.\n\nNo existing method grew in complexity, and the heavy per-digit logic lives in a fresh class with essentially no surrounding context. `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` and the full suite pass.",
